    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$2.99 a burrito\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for the world\u0027s favorite curry you can eat with one hand. A jar of garam masala and a couple of cans of tomato do most of the work.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "Garam masala is the one spice that makes this taste like the restaurant, and a jar lasts for many batches, so buy it once and use it freely.",
                       "Tomato paste and canned diced tomatoes are the cheap backbone of the sauce, and this batch uses close to a full can of each, so nothing dries out in the fridge.",
                       "Greek yogurt stands in for cream here and shows up all over this batch, so buy the big tub for the best price per ounce.",
                       "Buy rice in the biggest bag you have room for. It is the cheapest calorie in this recipe and it keeps forever."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Whisk about a third of the Greek yogurt with half the garam masala, half the ginger, half the garlic and the turmeric. Coat the diced chicken breast and let it marinate at least 30 minutes.",
                    "Cook the rice until tender and set it aside.",
                    "Melt the butter in a large pan and cook the diced onion until soft and golden, then add the remaining garlic and ginger, the ground cumin, paprika and the rest of the garam masala and stir for a minute.",
                    "Stir in the tomato paste and diced tomatoes, season with the salt, and simmer 10 minutes until it thickens into a masala.",
                    "Sear the marinated chicken in a separate hot pan until charred and cooked through, then fold it into the masala with the remaining Greek yogurt to finish the sauce.",
                    "Weigh the rice and the masala chicken together, subtract the empty bowl, and divide by 14. Lay that much down each tortilla, fold in the sides and roll.",
                    "Wrap each burrito and portion into 14 containers."
                ],
    "portion_html":  "Weigh the rice and masala chicken together, subtract the empty bowl, and divide by 14 so each burrito carries the same curry. Each burrito holds \u003cstrong\u003e364 calories and 36 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e. Reheat wrapped, and the sauce keeps the rice soft.",
